@RestaurantReservation.API_HostAddress = http://localhost:5122

### Reports Healthy only when the database is reachable through RestaurantReservation.Db
GET {{RestaurantReservation.API_HostAddress}}/health
Accept: text/plain

### 404 as application/problem+json, showing that the framework's own errors take the same shape
GET {{RestaurantReservation.API_HostAddress}}/api/no-such-route

### Sign in, every seeded user has the password below; alice.turner is a manager, bob.cook a waiter.
# @name signIn
POST {{RestaurantReservation.API_HostAddress}}/api/tokens
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "alice.turner",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

@token = {{signIn.response.body.accessToken}}

### Every reservation in the system. Staff only — a customer gets 403 here.
GET {{RestaurantReservation.API_HostAddress}}/api/reservations?page=1&pageSize=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One reservation. A customer may read only their own; anyone else's reads as missing.
GET {{RestaurantReservation.API_HostAddress}}/api/reservations/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Book a table. The restaurant and the table capacity are derived, so they are not sent.
# @name createReservation
POST {{RestaurantReservation.API_HostAddress}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "tableId": 1,
  "reservationDate": "2027-09-09T19:00:00",
  "partySize": 2
}

### Replace it. A PUT replaces the whole reservation rather than patching part of it.
PUT {{RestaurantReservation.API_HostAddress}}/api/reservations/{{createReservation.response.body.reservationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "tableId": 2,
  "reservationDate": "2027-09-09T20:00:00",
  "partySize": 3
}

### Cancel it.
DELETE {{RestaurantReservation.API_HostAddress}}/api/reservations/{{createReservation.response.body.reservationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### RQ4.1 — every employee holding the Manager position. Staff only.
GET {{RestaurantReservation.API_HostAddress}}/api/employees/managers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### RQ4.2 — one customer's reservations. A customer may ask only for their own; staff for anyone's.
GET {{RestaurantReservation.API_HostAddress}}/api/reservations/customer/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### RQ4.3 — the orders placed on a reservation, each with its items and their menu items.
# Reservation 6 exists but has no orders: that answers 200 with totalCount 0, not 404.
GET {{RestaurantReservation.API_HostAddress}}/api/reservations/1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### RQ4.4 — the distinct menu items ordered within a reservation.
GET {{RestaurantReservation.API_HostAddress}}/api/reservations/1/menu-items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### RQ4.5 — an employee's order figures. Managers may read anyone's, others only their own.
# Employee 4 has taken no orders, and so reports zeros rather than 404.
GET {{RestaurantReservation.API_HostAddress}}/api/employees/1/statistics
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sign out, which revokes the token above by its 'jti' until it would have expired anyway.
DELETE {{RestaurantReservation.API_HostAddress}}/api/tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
